# Stage 05 — A/B/C/D pretranslation trials (GATE)

Read `metadata/book_specific_translation_research.md` and `metadata/style_profile.md`.
Follow `skills/expert-translation-quality/SKILL.md`.

Pick 3-5 representative source passages (per the sample plan). For each, write
`qa/pretranslation/source_NN.md` (the passage) and `qa/pretranslation/trial_NN.md`
containing:
1. source text
2. function/intent of the passage
3. literal-translation risks
4. key term choices
5. variant A — faithful
6. variant B — readable {{ target_lang }}
7. variant C — literary polish
8. variant D — final candidate
9. why D is best for the body
10. PASS or FAIL

Then write `qa/pretranslation/pretranslation_report.md` with an overall
conclusion line `result: PASS` or `result: FAIL`, and refine `style_profile.md`
with anything learned.

If the report concludes FAIL, revise the trials and retry. Do NOT proceed to
translation. Only the controller records the deterministic gate decision.

Exit condition: report concludes PASS, gate recorded PASS, state PRETRANSLATION_PASS.
